Subject: tests: replace removed unittest.assertEquals aliases
Origin: DHI-internal (DHI build harness)
Description: Debian 13 uses Python 3.13, where unittest.assertEquals is no
 longer available. Five asynchronous store, clear, and lookup callbacks in
 libsecret 0.21.7 still call that alias. Their AttributeError exceptions escape
 the unittest case, so Meson incorrectly reports the affected tests as passing
 even though their result assertions never run. Replace only those five calls
 with the supported assertEqual spelling; no production code is changed.
Reference: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/b0a6ede3d0bd6fa4ffe413ab4dfc1059201df25b
Upstream source: https://sources.debian.org/src/libsecret/0.21.7-1/libsecret/
Base tree:
 Package: libsecret 0.21.7-1
 Orig: https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/libs/libsecret/libsecret_0.21.7.orig.tar.xz
 SHA256: 6b452e4750590a2b5617adc40026f28d2f4903de15f1250e1d1c40bfd68ed55e
 Layout: libsecret-0.21.7
Files:
 libsecret/test-py-clear.py
 libsecret/test-py-lookup.py
 libsecret/test-py-store.py
Generation: DHI-authored mechanical compatibility patch generated against the
 Debian 0.21.7 orig tree by replacing the five assertEquals calls with
 assertEqual. It was not pulled from or augmented from an upstream patch.
Forwarded: not-needed (test compatibility with Debian 13 Python only)

--- a/libsecret/test-py-clear.py
+++ b/libsecret/test-py-clear.py
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ class TestRemove(unittest.TestCase):
 		def on_result_ready(source, result, unused):
 			loop.quit()
 			deleted = Secret.password_clear_finish(result)
-			self.assertEquals(True, deleted)
+			self.assertEqual(True, deleted)
 
 		Secret.password_clear(STORE_SCHEMA, { "number": "2", "string": "two" },
 		                      None, on_result_ready, None)
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@ class TestRemove(unittest.TestCase):
 		def on_result_ready(source, result, unused):
 			loop.quit()
 			deleted = Secret.password_clear_finish(result)
-			self.assertEquals(False, deleted)
+			self.assertEqual(False, deleted)
 
 		Secret.password_clear(STORE_SCHEMA, { "number": "7", "string": "five" },
 		                      None, on_result_ready, None)
